# Ruleset: Microsoft CDN
#
# Expects DIRECT.
#
# Update, download, Office delivery and certificate validation hosts. Must precede Platforms/Microsoft.list, whose suffixes would otherwise take them. update.code.visualstudio.com is the VS Code update check; measured at 1,056 direct flows with none failed in the 14 days to 2026-09-09.
#
# download.prss.microsoft.com is deliberately absent. Its mainland edges answer on the direct path and cap every connection near 455 kB/s, so a completed flow says nothing about how long it took. Measured 2026-11-14 on the 389MB VS Code archive from vscode.download.prss.microsoft.com: 458 kB/s direct on one connection, 455 kB/s on each of four in parallel, against 58 and 89MB/s through a Singapore exit. The cap held on China Mobile, China Telecom and China Unicom edges, and playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com ran at the same rate. VS Code's own update took 31 minutes that day, 16 of them on an edge that delivered 20kB. The zone falls through to Platforms/Microsoft.list, so it is fast only while that file is bound to a proxy policy.

DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cdn.office.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,sfx.ms
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,windowsupdate.com
DOMAIN,az764295.vo.msecnd.net
DOMAIN,crl.microsoft.com
